# __NAME__

**__TAGLINE__** By [NativeCompute](https://nativecompute.net).

Built on [NCF](https://github.com/NativeCompute/ncf), the NativeCompute Framework.

## Installing

Download the latest build from [Releases](https://github.com/__REPO__/releases):

- **macOS** 11 or newer, Apple Silicon or Intel — paste this into Terminal:

  ```bash
  curl -fsSL https://github.com/__REPO__/releases/latest/download/install-macos.sh | bash
  ```

  It installs `__NAME__.app` in Applications. Run it again to update; add
  `-s -- --uninstall` after `bash` to remove it. The release also has
  `__SLUG__-<version>-macos-universal.zip`; a copy downloaded with a browser
  needs *Open Anyway* in System Settings → Privacy & Security the first time.
- **Linux** — unpack `__SLUG__-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` and run `./install.sh`.
- **Windows** — unpack `__SLUG__-<version>-windows-x86_64.zip` and run `__SLUG__.exe`.

From source: `./install.sh` builds and installs it for your user. On a Mac it
needs Apple's command line tools (`xcode-select --install`) and Rust, and
builds `__NAME__.app`.

## Development

```bash
cargo run
cargo test
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo run -- --emit-icon packaging/__SLUG__.svg
cargo run -- --emit-ico packaging/__SLUG__.ico
```

Releases: publish a release named `vX.Y.Z` on GitHub (or push the tag) and the release workflow attaches the Linux, macOS and Windows builds. `packaging/macos/bundle.sh` builds the Mac app on a Mac.

